{% if typecheck %}
Fix every type error by making the DATA match the declared contract. Follow these rules strictly:

ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN — a patch doing any of these is rejected and thrown away:
- Deleting, commenting out, or replacing a component usage to silence its error. If `<CredentialStrip items={...} />` has the wrong item shape, KEEP `<CredentialStrip>` and fix the items.
- Replacing real data with an empty array (`items={[]}`, `rows: []`), `null`, `undefined`, or a placeholder. An empty section is a WORSE defect than a type error.
- `as any`, `as unknown`, `: any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, `@ts-nocheck`, or non-null `!` spam. Type suppression is not a fix.
- Removing props, headings, or copy that carry business meaning.

HOW TO FIX EACH KIND OF ERROR:
- Wrong item/prop shape (TS2322, TS2739, TS2740, TS2345): RENAME AND REMAP the existing fields onto the declared ones, preserving all real content. `{ label: 'Since 2009', value: '15 years' }` for `CredentialStripItem { title: string; detail: string }` becomes `{ title: 'Since 2009', detail: '15 years' }` — same words, correct keys. Never drop an item.
- Missing required prop (TS2741): add it with real, business-specific content (a real image key from the images object, a real headline) — never `''` and never a lorem placeholder.
- Property does not exist on the source object (TS2339, TS2551): either the property must be ADDED to that object in `src/data/mock.ts` with real content of the right type, or the reader must use a key that genuinely exists. If a page reads `images.artwork1..artwork10` and the images object has only `hero`/`card1`/`card2`/`card3`, add those keys to the images object reusing the real URLs already present — never point an `<img>` at `undefined` and never delete the gallery.
- Unknown property in an object literal (TS2353): drop only that one unsupported key, or move its content into a supported key. Keep the object.
- Duplicate object key (TS1117): merge the two literals so no declared content is lost.
- Implicit `any` parameter (TS7006): annotate with the real element type from the declaration above — do NOT write `any`.
- Calling `.map()` on an object: iterate the correct array field on that object (e.g. `seed.kpis`), do not empty the section.
- A prop that does not exist on the component (`target`, `children` on a component with no children, an unsupported `variant` value): remove only that prop or switch to a declared variant value from the contract; keep the component and its content.

The declarations above are authoritative — do not guess field names when a declaration is shown.
